{"title":"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 30","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_30\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 30</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Roots_of_Unity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Roots of Unity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_30\">Problem 30</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 30\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/253e705a8e204ef0e7258e6148cc37d21debe6e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\cos 36^{\\circ} - \\cos 72^{\\circ}$\" width=\"161\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/c/3cc2f9498bbbccc16dbe42bec70ed992bdf6338e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 3-\\sqrt{6} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 2\\sqrt{3}-3\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"545\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the difference to product identity, we find that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/253e705a8e204ef0e7258e6148cc37d21debe6e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\cos 36^{\\circ} - \\cos 72^{\\circ}$\" width=\"161\" height=\"13\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae23d27c256c2d84f9e2a1fb9ffd075679f06f98.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\text{-}2\\sin{\\frac{(36^{\\circ}+72^{\\circ})}{2}}\\sin{\\frac{(36^{\\circ}-72^{\\circ})}{2}} \\implies\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/3/0136748f3bb6d1248587d4b4f704770bac46aa78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\text{-}2\\sin54^{\\circ}\\sin(\\text{-}18^{\\circ}).\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"18\" /> \nSince sine is an odd function, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b277f70da8546895c442b42f3f236e860470808a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{(\\text{-}18^{\\circ})}= \\text{-} \\sin{18^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/4/1d4eb7d2bc32aef2bfe96530b976f21659861571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{-}2\\sin54^{\\circ}\\sin(\\text{-}18^{\\circ})=2\\sin54^{\\circ}\\sin18^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"279\" height=\"18\" />. Using the property <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/8/f082a5b34a0a7616316a930b0f35cb69d9e2000e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{(90^{\\circ}-a)}=\\cos{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />, we find\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/926acc6dfca36c2165673800c2bb2ed92b40516c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=2\\cos(90^{\\circ}-54^{\\circ})\\cos(90^{\\circ}-18^{\\circ}) \\implies\\]\" width=\"312\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd91e28fd1e09737e1e788c59f4b595abb1bd50a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=2\\cos36^{\\circ}\\cos72^{\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"13\" />\nWe multiply the entire expression by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28826c2c77a49ab6013467ab2e2a7b06687a2af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin36^{\\circ}$\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> and use the double angle identity of sine twice to find\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/3/013bca6efb685939d3a105340569b8d4533bc7ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\sin36^{\\circ}=2\\sin36^{\\circ}\\cos36^{\\circ}\\cos72^{\\circ} \\implies\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c6f8b0121029c1a98cd594b2839dd96241a07d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\sin36^{\\circ}=\\sin72^{\\circ}\\cos72^{\\circ} \\implies\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a14edfa1710c5ca0a70bb77bc354bc5d2dd97041.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\sin36^{\\circ}=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin144^{\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"37\" />\nUsing the property <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58acb46ee48169c49a54cee3d267f7c80528a90c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(180^{\\circ}-a)=\\sin{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/138c11b6006a9c696c02fe8129d62e5467c23173.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin144^{\\circ}=\\sin36^{\\circ}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"139\" height=\"13\" /> Substituting this back into the equation, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/9/4b922a1340bbc27ab43c2c7cbe81a7b390f8faaf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\sin36^{\\circ}=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin36^{\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"37\" />\nDividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28826c2c77a49ab6013467ab2e2a7b06687a2af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin36^{\\circ}$\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8dc87509262c16a69ef2475d89d03c5e838bae0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}}\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24b827998def193fbf2d8ec73227dc09a0a27e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$72^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> is twice of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d0d9b28b429ef7a98b6ac8e14b6151af91ed33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, so evaluating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/6/50650d985ccf86f4f76894aa27f0020773f015bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 36^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> and using the double angle identify is enough to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b0d8240bfc42981c536983a3a9aca087b6d7077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 36^{\\circ} - \\cos 72^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" /> \n</p><p>We first let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16e29eaab333491ff421e3ac830da6dcdb4a108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\cos 36^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />. \nNotice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09eb34bee840e619cf24e488cec532fc81cce8e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36^{\\circ}/4 = 9^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d441febd25096e7f976f4c1f576c6021933b27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36^{\\circ} = 45^{\\circ} - 9^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"16\" />. \nRewriting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/6/50650d985ccf86f4f76894aa27f0020773f015bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 36^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc8e326904a85fd2534e5100b012b63f1a3e9e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos (45^{\\circ} - 9^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />, we then use the difference of angles identify to find \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c578eb77f719fd3064e73630bc0f63d37b9e579.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = \\cos 36^{\\circ} = \\cos (45^{\\circ} - 9^{\\circ}) = \\cos 45^{\\circ}\\cos 9^{\\circ} - \\sin 45^{\\circ}\\sin 9^{\\circ} = \\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}(\\cos 9^{\\circ} - \\sin 9^{\\circ})\\]\" width=\"607\" height=\"41\" /> \nRearranged to get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/d/21d57d5bf9639c0ab67e3da5124316079a9188bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt2 n = \\cos 9^{\\circ} - \\sin 9^{\\circ}\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" />\nUsing the half-angle identify twice, and noticing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf008d90a5320a143daeb70e93054a9e43c394c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 9^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> is positive, we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39d7e56da121efc718e1733252876631d30e744e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos 9^{\\circ} = \\cos \\frac{18^{\\circ}}{2} = \\sqrt \\frac{1 + \\cos 18^{\\circ}}{2} = \\sqrt \\frac{1 + \\sqrt \\frac{1 + \\cos 36^{\\circ}}{2}}{2}\\]\" width=\"413\" height=\"63\" />\nAlso, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9b7c9b67279842bf1f08009530fb3b73208860d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin 9^{\\circ} = \\sqrt {1 - \\cos^2 9} = \\sqrt {1 - \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{\\frac{1 + 36^{\\circ}}{2}}}{2}} = \\sqrt {\\frac{1 - \\sqrt{\\frac{1 + 36^{\\circ}}{2}}}{2}}\\]\" width=\"462\" height=\"63\" />\n</p><p>Thus we can get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea2f306ff90f6db7387f2f547dd1c6e834517a74.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt2 n = \\sqrt \\frac{1 + \\sqrt \\frac{1 + \\cos 36^{\\circ}}{2}}{2} - \\sqrt {\\frac{1 - \\sqrt{\\frac{1 + 36^{\\circ}}{2}}}{2}}\\]\" width=\"326\" height=\"63\" />\nSquaring both sides and simplifying, this results in \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c5b4cf27767b03c47f1467aecf98c9b591b212e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2n^2 = 1 - \\sqrt{\\frac{1-n}{2}}\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"43\" />\nFrom which we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/2/202aa2dcda3f46e4a11a6931cf77b07ee7f777d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2n^2 - 1 = - \\sqrt{\\frac{1-n}{2}}\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"43\" />\nSquaring both sides again, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f305bf2ea5d4e9c078d7810fad8967f23928fe48.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4n^4 - 4n^2 +1 = \\frac{1-n}{2}\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"37\" />\nMultiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and rearranging, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f45dcf5f445e5fbdb97879f62cc097d28a9a19.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8n^4 - 8n^2 + n + 1 = 0\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"17\" />\nFactoring out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe64129fe00ec02144befbe2469dd5cb03b6c10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"17\" /> from the first two terms and applying difference of squares, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0cbc185525800dc2bfdf8074c96a393727c4b93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8n^2(n+1)(n-1) + n+1 = 0\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"20\" /> \nWe know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16e29eaab333491ff421e3ac830da6dcdb4a108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\cos 36^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" /> which is not equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, so we divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/b/a6b97b58f425a1604bdbb3ecccca56affaff7f6c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8n^3 -8n^2 +1 = 0\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"17\" />\nUsing the rational root test, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0a7983635e3b90ea24ba3512c9d1c66714a9ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" /> is a solution of this equation. However, we also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/6/50650d985ccf86f4f76894aa27f0020773f015bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 36^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> is not equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, so we divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/6018deb638262d22057665d88d7e3e7b70188cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n- \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" /> to get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/0/570a7c2da2abb987dc9ff8965fcc36fa04206d20.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8n^2 - 4n - 2 = 0\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"15\" /> \nUsing the quadratic formula, we find that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76a54ae2b69fae07503582e8a0ee49fee40df90d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = \\frac{1 \\pm \\sqrt{5}}{4}\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"41\" /> \nWe know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be positive, which gives us \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4a34e0e9d0a7620d713a8485dfa924c09062c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{5}}{4}\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Thus, using the double angle identify, we can find \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3bf6a158a092726ddd7b7f17054bdb145c31bc0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\cos 36^{\\circ} - \\cos 72^{\\circ} = \\cos 36^{\\circ} - 2\\cos^2 36^{\\circ} + 1 = n - 2n^2 + 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\frac{1}{2}}\\]\" width=\"540\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>-SaraLiu24\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Roots_of_Unity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Roots_of_Unity)\">Solution 3 (Roots of Unity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Roots of Unity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63d67a02700507f7b9859848010ea0f1e07ce7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = \\cos 72^\\circ - i \\sin 72^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is a fifth root of unity, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc7db3b780dd6c6ac6b4611b48e49c1d78faa8d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w^5 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/8/bd87248bd4d69b819996641a5edecc4ed7bc6030.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w^5-1 = (w-1)(w^4 + w^3 + w^2 + w + 1) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"359\" height=\"21\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/800b728600678b6b1ab666ef97e998ef60faf5bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w - 1 \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c09d85a9c5cd9d4bff5dea6d94048fb20fe5a33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w^4 + w^3 + w^2 + w + 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"210\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Both the real and imaginary parts of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93ad054af54b7ed01ba151280b129aefd9265d0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w^4 + w^3 + w^2 + w + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" /> must be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the real part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93ad054af54b7ed01ba151280b129aefd9265d0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w^4 + w^3 + w^2 + w + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" /> can also be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/593b4c4ba4c68ffaa7136b0993be7a3550803930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 288^\\circ + \\cos 216^\\circ + \\cos 144^\\circ + \\cos 72^\\circ + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"340\" height=\"16\" />.  Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/a/dba456fa3b4461e3f75e971fc470b747da94a984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 288^\\circ = \\cos 72^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"142\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/b/d7b15d9c778ebd374d537e81e900bcb49f301b74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 216^\\circ = \\cos 144^\\circ = -\\cos 36^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"245\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e042ae507c64fafde335575d9a3244527bbb86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 288^\\circ + \\cos 216^\\circ + \\cos 144^\\circ + \\cos 72^\\circ + 1 = \\cos 72^\\circ - \\cos 36^\\circ - \\cos 36^\\circ + \\cos 72^\\circ + 1 = 2(\\cos 72^\\circ - \\cos 36^\\circ) + 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"916\" height=\"20\" />.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87b9402ba7cc8069f03de4f587cb0837de2e18cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 72^\\circ - \\cos 36^\\circ = -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"182\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b4bc0b5c07cfdc3c8207d10475756fed1fa35ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 36^\\circ - \\cos 72^\\circ = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"213\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME\" title=\"1975 AHSME\">1975 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1975 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1975\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a h